# Normalize line endings to LF in the repo regardless of the checkout OS,
# so a Windows checkout doesn't turn every existing file into a full-file
# diff the moment it's saved. Without this, ~4,000 already-committed article
# files show as "modified" on Windows purely from CRLF vs LF — no content
# change, just noise that would bury real diffs in every future commit.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary/media — never touch line endings, never diff as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.svg binary
*.ico binary
*.mp4 binary
*.mp3 binary
*.wav binary
